[B]ALS: Anti-Lag System[/B]
Anti-lag on every turbocharged car BeamNG ships.

Source: [URL='https://github.com/AyQWERTY/beamng-als']github.com/AyQWERTY/beamng-als[/URL]
If you want the [B]cars from other mods[/B], build the mod yourself from the source above.

The mod adds one function: anti-lag. Everything else about the turbo stays as it was. Vanilla anti-lag parts have their power written into jbeam; here it is calculated from that turbo's own wastegate pressure and pressure curve, which lands on the same kind of numbers.

[MEDIA=youtube]5gnrHvG4MQY[/MEDIA]

[B]Controls[/B]
[LIST]
[*][B]K[/B] - Toggle ALS. Default is on.
[*][B]NumPad +[/B] - Scramble. Toggle: raises the boost set point for an overboost until pressed again.
[*][B]U[/B] - Rolling anti-lag. Hold to keep anti-lag running while driving.
[*][B];[/B] - Rolling launch. The rev cut jumps to the RPM the engine is at, and anti-lag is forced on.
[/LIST]

The four actions sit under [B]Vehicle Specific (installed parts)[/B] in Settings -> Controls.
[ATTACH]1353422[/ATTACH]

They also show up in the in-game bindings legend:
[ATTACH]1350553[/ATTACH]

[B]Parts[/B]
The mod ships an ALS variant of the engine-management part of every turbocharged car. It is installed like any other part, under [B]Engine Management[/B] in the vehicle config.
[ATTACH]1353596[/ATTACH]

[B]Tuning[/B]
[LIST]
[*][B]Scramble overboost[/B] - 0 to 30 psi added while the scramble key is active (default 10). If the turbo already sits at its physical ceiling and cannot spin faster, the extra pressure will not appear, or will be smaller than the slider says.
[*][B]Wastegate pressure[/B] - raises the pressure the wastegate holds, up to the top of that turbo's own curve. It only shows up where the stock part has no wastegate slider.
[/LIST]
[ATTACH]1353597[/ATTACH]
